WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.833
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for the words that will not stay.

2
00:00:04.283 --> 00:00:12.238
The goal: on day ten, your child reads sixteen of the most common words, alone, and inside sentences never seen before.

3
00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:19.502
That is the goal. It is not a promise. This video tells you what the plan is, what to expect, and how to use it.

4
00:00:20.302 --> 00:00:26.883
This plan is for a child who can sound out short words, but cannot hold on to words like the, was, and said.

5
00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:29.914
The word is known today, and it is gone tomorrow.

6
00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:33.593
Or it is known on a card, but not inside a sentence.

7
00:00:34.043 --> 00:00:38.328
That is common at five and six. It is not a sign that something is wrong.

8
00:00:38.778 --> 00:00:45.664
A card asks a child to remember a word as a picture. Short words look alike, so there is little to hold on to.

9
00:00:46.264 --> 00:00:49.993
This plan ties each word to its sounds instead. Watch.

10
00:00:50.493 --> 00:00:51.642
Said. Three sounds.

11
00:00:55.031 --> 00:00:59.867
The first letter and the last letter play fair. They say just what your child was taught.

12
00:01:00.317 --> 00:01:04.237
Only the middle part has to be known by heart. We call it the heart part.

13
00:01:04.687 --> 00:01:08.131
One small part is much less to remember than a whole word.

14
00:01:08.931 --> 00:01:13.436
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

15
00:01:13.886 --> 00:01:19.421
Day one is a short check. It shows you where the trouble is. Day ten shows you what changed.

16
00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:25.128
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

17
00:01:25.578 --> 00:01:30.345
On four of the days there is a sound track for your child. You press play and step away.

18
00:01:31.145 --> 00:01:37.186
Now, what to expect. One small group of words a day. Words that share a heart part are taught together.

19
00:01:37.636 --> 00:01:43.650
Forgetting is the trouble. So no word is taught once and left. The earlier words come back, every day.

20
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.933
Some days will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

21
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:52.412
On day ten, the check gives you one of three next steps.

22
00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:59.699
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

23
00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:04.717
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

24
00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:08.315
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

25
00:02:08.765 --> 00:02:13.036
Then your child carries on with the page, and reads three words to you at the end.

26
00:02:13.836 --> 00:02:19.710
Put the Words I Own chart where your child can see it. A word read right away earns a colored box.

27
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.441
You need the printed pages, a pencil, and a red crayon for the hearts.

28
00:02:24.891 --> 00:02:30.103
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about three minutes.
